<title>USA: No need for immediate US move on American-Lindsey.</title>
<headline>No need for immediate US move on American-Lindsey.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A top White House official said late on Friday that as long as American Airlines and its pilots are negotiating, there is no immediate need for President Bill Clinton to intervene in their labour dispute.</p>
<p>&quot;As long as they're making progress ... there's no need for us to act,&quot; White House Deputy Counsel Bruce Lindsey told reporters. Asked if the parties, American's parent AMR Corp and the Allied Pilots' Association union, were making progress, Lindsey replied only: &quot;They're still talking.&quot;</p>
</text>
